A||N||4||rigdonhome||The Unique Beauty of a Fast-Moving Fiero||||10||
Z||000000||rigdonhome||12-24-2001||01:45 AM||||Fieronians!<P>I am the proud owner of a sweet '88 Black GT in very prestine condition...  I drive it to work every day, and soon the weather will confine it to the garage for a few months...  <P>I was Christmas shopping last night and therefore was piloting the Family Truckster, a '92 Chevrolet Full-Size High-Top Conversion Van powered by a TBI 350.  For a 6,000-Pound, Brick-o-Dynamic, Stock Vehicle with 120,000 miles on it, it moves right along with far more Charasmatic Torque and Growl than you might expect such a Behemoth to...  A stomp on the GO pedal is nothing like stomping the Fiero's GO pedal, but it still brings a grin to my face each and every time...<P>Well, it was dark and drizzling last night on the interstate (3 lanes at this point) and as I used my intimidating size to urge lifeless slugs out of the fast lane so that I could continue my 80mph flight home, I eventually came up behind an '85 or '86 GT (Black, I think...) that was also trapped behind some slow (undoubtedly in the mind as well as on the road) motorists who were blocking the Fast Lane.  Now, there may be those of you who think that I had no business being in the Fast Lane in my 6,000-pound, 8-foot tall School Bus!  Well, let me assure you that I NEVER impede the flow of traffic, and I always enjoy the stunned looks on peoples' faces when I blow by them at 90mph in my Mobile Living Room.<P>So anyway, I admired the Fiero in front of me  while he and I both waited for the Blue-Hair in front of him to get out of the way and let us rise to an acceptable cruising altitude once again...  The incredible size difference (more than twice in this case!!!) between my Van and the Fiero now in front of me made me realize how small the Fiero really is!  No wonder it is so quick with even a stock 2.8L, and an absolute Rocket with a Small Block in it!<P>Finally, the lifeless drone behind the wheel of the Buick which was impeding our progress gave in and got out of the way...  His pulse must have finally stopped completely and caused him to slump over, and therefore veer to the right.  <P>Just as I would have had it been ME behind the wheel of MY Fiero waiting impatiently for a Blue-Hair to stop blocking the fast lane (and in fact, as I DID even though I was in the Truckster!), the Fiero driver stepped on it and quickly climbed to a safe cruising altitude of 80mph.  I did the same, admiring the tail of mist being formed from the wake of the Fiero...  Just to get a better look at the car in motion, I sped up and pulled along-side him in the center lane.  I was able to further admire the streamlined form of the Fiero from the side for about 4 or 5 seconds before its driver noticed that I had sped up to pace him...<P>He then put the hammer down and disappeared into the night and the swirling mist left behind him in the drizzle.<P>I rarely get to see a Fiero similar to mine in motion, let alone with all of the special effects provided last night by the drizzling weather conditions...  It was pretty damn cool!<P>Cheers,<BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>42,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Joe Torma||12-24-2001||02:00 AM||||Nice story  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I used to love driving alongside my friend who has an 85GT-it was basically like looking at my car an 86SE.  They sure are beautiful skimming the road.<P>And I used to like to watch [privlidged] people drive my car around.  That would always put a smile on my face, but alas, my car has been in 10,000 pieces for the longest time.<P>Oh and how 'bout glass front buildings...THE BEST!<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000002||artherd||12-24-2001||03:31 AM||||I really enjoy watching (and *hearing*) others drive my car.  Tursted individuals only of course. (a short list, qualification includes mid-engine car ownership  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It's so much fun to *hear* these cars driven to their limits in an autocross!<P>PS: Glass buildings rule!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Nice story   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I used to love driving alongside my friend who has an 85GT-it was basically like looking at my car an 86SE.  They sure are beautiful skimming the road.<P>And I used to like to watch [privlidged] people drive my car around.  That would always put a smile on my face, but alas, my car has been in 10,000 pieces for the longest time.<P>Oh and how 'bout glass front buildings...THE BEST!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||watts||12-24-2001||10:03 AM||||Glass building, tunnels, and tall cement walls on your side.<P>Gotta love the echo in a tunnel though.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mattyman||12-24-2001||02:12 PM||||I always wanted to see what my car looked like in action so I got someone to video tape me crusing along the road by my house.HaHa  It was nice to see my Fiero from the outside instead of the inside.  Shes a real beauty and looks alot different in motion than sitting still.  <P>------------------<BR>You gotta stand for Something or your gonna fall for everything.||||reg||1
